==============================================================================================================================
k03 -- THE EFE ENDING RADIUS:  r_EFE = sqrt(G M_b a_0)/g_ext = v_flat^2/g_ext
==============================================================================================================================

1. THE EXTERNAL FIELD, measured independently of any lensing, from 2M++
------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  175 lines of sight (the SPARC footprint, the programme's own external-field construction)
    e_N = g_N,ext/a_0  (no cluster term      ): median 3.823e-04  16-84 [1.73e-04, 6.29e-04]   ->  TRUE field g_ext/a_0 = nu(e_N) e_N: median 0.0197  16-84 [0.0132, 0.0254]
    e_N = g_N,ext/a_0  (maximal cluster term ): median 3.270e-03  16-84 [1.56e-03, 5.24e-03]   ->  TRUE field g_ext/a_0 = nu(e_N) e_N: median 0.0588  16-84 [0.0403, 0.0750]
  [PASS] K03.1 the repository's own 2M++ external fields put the TRUE external field on a field galaxy in the range 0.01-0.07 a_0.  This check fails if the file is being read in the wrong units, which would invalidate everything below   (2M++ no-cluster (median): 0.0197 a_0, 2M++ max-cluster (median): 0.0588 a_0, 2M++ no-cluster (16th pct, the most isolated): 0.0132 a_0)

